On 5 February 2016 at 08:27, Reshetova, Elena < =
<mailto:elena.reshetova@intel.com> elena.reshetova@intel.com> wrote:

I noticed that during the build bitbake supplies you rather correct (if =
it is correct in the recipe) list of recipe build-time dependencies. =
However, this isn=E2=80=99t true for run-time dependencies. Moreover it =
seems that when you define a recipe you don=E2=80=99t have to list =
run-time dependencies, but rather than package manager would figure it =
out.=20


>After do_package has run the dependencies will be correct, but until =
that point the runtime library dependencies won't have been extracted.

=20

Actually my task seems to run after do_package has already run, but I =
don=E2=80=99t have RDEPENDS filled with anything useful. How you =
supposed to query them from bitbake? I was trying these variants:=20

=20

recipe.r_deps =3D d.getVar('RDEPENDS_' +  <http://recipe.name> =
recipe.name, True)

=20

or even simple:

=20

recipe.r_deps =3D d.getVar('RDEPENDS=E2=80=99, True)

=20

Best Regards,
Elena.


